Original Zero native durability and bounded-wait extension, 0.11 candidate

Canonical compiler.zero adds two value primitives without a foreign compiler,
assembler, linker or runtime. Existing own build/zero compiled its source;
all three new generations are byte-identical. Seed promotion is root-owned.

filesync[handle]: Linux fsync with EINTR retry; Windows FlushFileBuffers.
Returns0/u64(-1), keeps the handle and offset. This is an OS file flush request,
not directory/rename durability, publisher authentication or proof of survival
after physical power loss. Portable callers use an owned writable regular file.

hostwait[milliseconds]: Linux nanosleep with remaining-time EINTR retry;
Windows Sleep. Inclusive bounds0..86400000, return0 or u64(-1). Invalid unsigned
inputs never sleep. It suspends the calling host thread and does not register
an automatic startup service or switch Zero cooperative workers.

Both guest targets accept these source forms, evaluate their operands and
return full-u64(-1) without a file operation or delay. Raw/EFI/real targets
reject the operations. Names are reserved in every target. Template IDs102/103,
builtin indices73/74, tokens573/574; metadata slots75. Existing memory-region
positions and4022880-byte reservation are unchanged. PE import table now has
25 entries plus a null entry (208 bytes); all RVAs remain unchanged.

The hostwait-*.hex files are original instruction data with labels. Existing
windows-author.zero, itself written in Zero, resolves those labels. The same
formatter's historical name does not make Linux output a Windows primitive;
canonical template banks and target conditions determine each target.
windows-layout.txt reproduces every Windows template value exactly.

Verification in this directory:
-selfhost.json: three identical native compiler generations;
-results.json:136 focused checks, including21 native assertions on Linux and
 Wine each, parser/arity/reserved-name gating, syscall argument observation,
 injected EINTR recovery and non-EINTR error reporting, actual x64 guest
 fallback execution, IA32 fallback compilation, native Windows self-rebuild;
-common-merged.json:433 existing common parser/backend/fallback regressions;
-linux-verification.json:17 existing native API behavior cases;
-windows-verification.json: existing61 API/20 boundary assertions and Unicode,
 argv, cooperative-worker, Ezero host-file and Windows selfhost regressions;
-guest-sizes.json: own compiler app64=94438, app32=124286, both within131072.

Windows results are Wine10 on Linux, not a native Microsoft Windows run.
strace is external test infrastructure used to inject EINTR/EIO/EFAULT;
it is not part of the product implementation or distributed runtime.
No real disk power-loss, native Windows reparse or physical hardware claim.
